config BR2_PACKAGE_EMBRA_LLAMA_CPP
	bool "embra-llama-cpp"
	depends on BR2_INSTALL_LIBSTDCPP
	depends on BR2_TOOLCHAIN_HAS_THREADS
	depends on !BR2_STATIC_LIBS
	depends on !BR2_PACKAGE_LLAMA_CPP
	help
	  The model server of native models (experimental): llama.cpp's
	  llama-server at the release embraOS pins, the version in
	  embra-llama-cpp.mk and the archive's sha256 in the hash file
	  beside it. embrad keeps one running on loopback while the
	  operator asked for a native model, and the brain is its one
	  client.

	  The server alone is built: no command-line tool, no web page,
	  no TLS and no download code. The CPU backends are libraries
	  under /usr/lib/llama-cpp, one for each instruction set, and
	  the server loads the one the processor can run.

	  Takes the place of Buildroot's llama-cpp package, whose recipe
	  names an older build without these options; the two would
	  install the same libraries, so only one is selected.

	  https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp
